# TODO: authenticity check

The TV is on low in the next room while you study. Something about floods somewhere, and then something about a shooting.
{GameState.parent_word} stops mid-paragraph to listen, then turns back to you with a kind of calm. "You see? Men will be lovers of themselves. Just like Paul said. Right on schedule."
- Nod.
	[signal arg="CONVICTION:1"]
	You nod. It's a comfort, the way everything fits. {GameState.parent_word} finds the place again with one finger.
- "Didn't they say that about the news when you were my age, too?" | [if DoubtMeter.noticing >= 25] [else=disable alt_text=""]
	[signal arg="EXPOSE:1.5"]
	[signal arg="STANDING:family:-2"]
	{GameState.parent_word} looks at you over their reading glasses for a long moment.
	"We're closer now than we've ever been," they say, gently, as if you'd asked the time. "That's all."
	They turn the TV off.
